<article class="env-example" id="310767">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/310767">Example <span data-tag="310767">5.1.6.9</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be the $\infty $-category $\SSet $ of spaces. Then an object $C \in \SSet $ is completely compact if and only if it is equivalent to $\ast $, the final object of $\SSet $. </p>
